  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-312d6ee7-41d3-42ce-b8dc-1c86eb08e122-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Dungeons &amp; Dragons is a tabletop role-playing game in which players portray adventurers in a shared fantasy world. A Dungeon Master describes situations, plays other characters, and adjudicates the rules, while the group decides how to explore, negotiate, fight, and solve problems. Dice introduce uncertainty, but much of the activity takes place through conversation and collective imagination."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-312d6ee7-41d3-42ce-b8dc-1c86eb08e122-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Created by Gary Gygax and Dave Arneson and first published by TSR in 1974, D&amp;D grew from miniature wargaming into a model for sustained character-based campaigns. Its many editions change particular mechanics, while retaining the interplay between written rules and a group’s unfolding story."
    },
